{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>The tribe of Zebulun</b> — and it does not say 'and the tribe of,' as it says regarding the others, because Zebulun supported Issachar. And I saw in the Tanḥuma the reason that it does not say 'and the tribe of' regarding Zebulun as it says regarding all of them — to teach you that Zebulun engaged in commerce and placed food into the mouth of Issachar. Therefore Scripture did not wish to make him subordinate to him, to say that his reward is as great as his. And thus it says: 'It is a tree of life to those who hold it, and its supporters are happy' (Proverbs 3:18), and it is written: 'For in the shadow of wisdom, in the shadow of money' (Ecclesiastes 7:12). Therefore all are reckoned as one tribe, as if it said: Issachar — the tribe of Zebulun."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:21:04.962009269Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}